WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.064
The school assigns these readings to vascular access and the ECG introduction. We will use them to explain one complete chain: what enters the circulation, how the heart moves it and how tissues receive what they need.
学校把这些阅读放在血管通路及ECG入门周。我们用它们解释一条完整链：什么进入循环，心脏如何推动，以及组织怎样获得所需。

00:00:14.064 --> 00:00:28.296
An IV is not successful care just because a catheter is in a vein. A tracing is not successful assessment just because the machine prints it. Both must contribute to understanding and helping the patient.
导管进入静脉，不等于照护已成功；机器打出记录，不等于评估已成功。两者都必须帮助理解并照护患者。

00:00:28.296 --> 00:00:41.064
The paired reading panels cover the named blood, heart and vascular domains and the assigned nursing page spans. Their source maps distinguish an internal page match from a confirmed school edition.
中英阅读面板涵盖具名血液、心脏、血管领域及指定护理页段。来源图会区分候选内部页码匹配，与已确认学校版本这两件事。

00:00:41.064 --> 00:00:53.496
Follow the original patient throughout this lesson, then use the practical lesson to demonstrate the route and the ECG lessons to measure the signal. The old Nancy website is not a prerequisite.
沿本课原创患者学下去，再到实训课演示通路，到ECG课测信号。不需要先学旧Nancy网站课程。

00:00:53.496 --> 00:01:55.584
Read the assigned extent first, then the labelled supporting explanation. In the recovered course-folder copy, Blood covers 18.1-18.6 and Key Terms; Heart covers 19.2-19.3 plus the 19.4 objectives and opening cardiac-output/stroke-volume text on printed 788. Heart 19.1, the rest of 19.4 and 19.5 below are supporting context, not additional assigned pages. Vessels covers 20.1-20.4 and only the 20.5 objectives/introductory paragraph on printed 842; detailed systemic routes and 20.6 below are supporting context. A section heading on the last assigned page does not assign the entire following section. The school focus is explaining osmotic versus hydrostatic pressure, then applying the delivery chain to vascular access and ECGs.
先读指定范围，再读明确标记的辅助解释。找回的课程副本中，血液包括18.1至18.6及关键词；心脏包括19.2至19.3，以及印刷788页的19.4学习目标和开头心排量、每搏量正文。下文19.1、19.4其余内容及19.5属于辅助背景，不是新增指定页。血管包括20.1至20.4，以及印刷842页20.5的学习目标和引言段；下文详细体循环路线及20.6属于辅助背景。指定末页出现某节标题，不等于整节后文都列入阅读。学校重点是解释渗透压与静水压，再把输送链用于血管通路及ECG。

00:01:55.584 --> 00:02:50.832
Keep the textbook proportions tied to their denominator. Its simplified adult sample is about 45 percent red cells, less than 1 percent buffy coat and the remainder plasma; plasma itself is approximately 92 percent water, 7 percent proteins and 1 percent other solutes. Those plasma percentages are not percentages of whole blood. For an original 100 mL sample with 45 mL packed red cells and about 55 mL plasma, 92 percent of 55 is about 50.6 mL plasma water, not 92 mL. The source adult blood-volume averages are about 5-6 L for males and 4-5 L for females, roughly 8 percent of body weight; these are population teaching examples, not a measured individual volume or a hemorrhage replacement formula.
教材比例必须连同分母记。简化成人血样约45%为红细胞，白膜层少于1%，其余为血浆；血浆本身约92%水、7%蛋白、1%其他溶质。这些血浆百分比不是全血百分比。原创100mL血样若有45mL压积红细胞、约55mL血浆，则55的92%约为50.6mL血浆水，不是92mL。来源成人血容量平均例约为男性5至6L、女性4至5L，约占体重8%；这是人群教学例，不是个体实测血容量或失血补液公式。

00:02:50.832 --> 00:03:06.504
Consider an original fifty-eight-year-old with vomiting, poor intake and dizziness. The pulse is rapid, the skin feels cool and the pressure is lower than the person usually reports. The patient can answer but looks increasingly tired.
设一名原创58岁患者，呕吐、少进食并头晕。脉快、皮肤凉，血压比其自述平常低。虽能回答，却越来越疲惫。

00:03:06.504 --> 00:03:19.248
The pulse oximeter reads ninety-seven percent with a usable waveform. This is information about saturation, not proof that enough hemoglobin is present or enough blood is reaching tissues.
指氧仪为97%，波形可用。这是饱和度信息，不证明血红蛋白够，也不证明足量血流抵达组织。

00:03:19.248 --> 00:03:33.240
Vomiting makes volume loss plausible, but bleeding, infection, cardiac problems, medicines and metabolic illness remain possible. Do not decide the whole story before taking the history and examining the patient.
呕吐使失液合理，但出血、感染、心脏问题、药物及代谢病仍可能。病史检查尚未完成，不能先把整件事定死。

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:46.440
Our task is to explain which link may be failing, what additional evidence matters and what a justified intervention should change. This is a simulation for reasoning, not an automatic fluid order.
任务是解释哪环可能失败、还需什么证据，以及有理由的干预应改变什么。这是推理模拟，不是自动补液医嘱。

00:03:46.440 --> 00:04:00.216
Start at an appropriate peripheral vein. Venous blood returns toward the right atrium and crosses the tricuspid valve into the right ventricle. The pulmonary valve guards outflow toward the pulmonary arteries and lungs.
从合适的外周静脉起，血向右房回流，经三尖瓣进右室，再通过肺动脉瓣进入肺动脉和肺。

00:04:00.216 --> 00:04:13.008
After pulmonary gas exchange, pulmonary veins carry blood to the left atrium. It crosses the mitral valve into the left ventricle, then the aortic valve into the systemic arterial circuit.
肺气体交换后，肺静脉把血带到左房，经二尖瓣到左室，再过主动脉瓣进入体动脉循环。

00:04:13.008 --> 00:04:27.936
Arteries are named for moving away from the heart, not for a mandatory oxygen level. Pulmonary arteries and veins make that distinction clear. Diagram colors are conventions; venous blood is not literally blue.
动脉按离开心脏命名，不按必须含多少氧。肺动静脉清楚说明这个区别。图上颜色只是惯例，静脉血并不真是蓝色。

00:04:27.936 --> 00:04:40.800
An administered product can therefore affect distant tissues, not just the insertion site. A blocked, contaminated or misplaced route interrupts this intended chain even if the syringe empties.
给入产品因此能影响远处组织，不只穿刺处。通路若堵、污染或错位，即使注射器空了，也没保证完成预期链条。

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:56.520
Blood has a liquid matrix and suspended formed elements. Plasma includes water, albumin, globulins, fibrinogen and other substances. Red cells, white cells and platelets are not dissolved plasma electrolytes.
血有液态基质及悬浮有形成分。血浆含水、白蛋白、球蛋白、纤维蛋白原等。红白细胞和血小板不是溶在血浆里的电解质。

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:09.912
Red cells provide hemoglobin carriage, white cells support defense, and platelets with coagulation proteins help control bleeding. A fluid that increases volume does not replace every one of these functions.
红细胞提供血红蛋白携氧，白细胞支持防御，血小板与凝血蛋白帮助止血。增加容量的液体，并不替代全部功能。

00:05:09.912 --> 00:05:24.480
Hematocrit is the red-cell volume fraction, while hemoglobin concentration is a different measurement. Both are affected by context and changes in plasma volume; neither alone is a real-time meter of recent blood loss.
红细胞比容是红细胞体积分数，血红蛋白浓度是另一测量。两者都受背景及血浆量改变影响，均不能独自当即时失血量计。

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:37.176
The assigned reading explains the lineages, cell functions and hemostatic chain in detail. Link each component to a clinical role instead of memorizing a list of percentages without a purpose.
指定导读详述谱系、细胞功能及止血链。应把每个成分连到临床作用，而不是无目的背一串百分比。

00:05:37.176 --> 00:05:52.800
Adult marrow continually produces blood elements. Myeloid and lymphoid branches give rise to different descendants, and growth-factor signals regulate production. This is the biology behind a marrow space with an active vascular connection.
成人骨髓不断产生血液成分，髓系和淋巴系形成不同后代，生长因子调生成。这也说明骨髓空间有活跃血管连接。

00:05:52.800 --> 00:06:07.368
EPO supports later red-cell production when renal tissue senses reduced oxygen availability. It does not immediately restore circulation in a vomiting or bleeding patient. Physiological compensation has a time course.
肾组织可得氧减少时，EPO支持后续造红细胞，却不能立即恢复呕吐或出血患者循环。生理代偿有时间过程。

00:06:07.368 --> 00:06:20.064
An appropriate IO catheter accesses marrow vascular channels. It is not an injection into a sealed bone cavity, and apparent needle stability alone does not prove usable placement or safe delivery.
合适IO导管进入骨髓血管通道，不是注入封闭骨腔。针看似稳固，仍不能证明位置可用或给入安全。

00:06:20.064 --> 00:06:33.960
Use the practical lesson for current PCP indications, on-scene supervision, age limits, site/device checks and failed-attempt rules. Knowing the route exists does not remove any of those requirements.
当前PCP指征、现场督导、年龄限制、部位器材检查及失败次数规则，详见实训课。知道这条路存在，不会取消这些要求。

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:46.848
A useful mental model is that oxygen delivery depends on oxygen content multiplied by blood flow. Saturation is one contributor to content; hemoglobin amount is another major contributor.
有用模型是氧输送取决于氧含量乘血流。饱和度是氧含量的一项，血红蛋白多少是另一重要项。

00:06:46.848 --> 00:07:02.496
A nearly full small truck carries less than a nearly full large truck. Similarly, a high saturation with very little hemoglobin does not represent normal oxygen-carrying capacity. The oximeter does not measure the size of that truck.
几乎装满的小车，仍可能比几乎装满的大车载得少。同样，血红蛋白很少时，即使饱和度高，携氧能力也未正常；指氧仪不测这辆车有多大。

00:07:02.496 --> 00:07:15.456
The truck must also move. Very low output or obstructed regional flow can impair delivery despite acceptable saturation. Electrical activity on the monitor cannot establish that movement either.
车还得能走。即使饱和度尚可，低心排或局部血流受阻也可损害输送。监护电活动同样不能证明这辆车在走。

00:07:15.456 --> 00:07:29.472
Return to the original patient: ninety-seven percent does not cancel cool skin, altered perfusion or deteriorating awareness. Assess the whole chain and the trend rather than reassuring yourself with its best number.
回到原创患者：97%不能抵消皮肤凉、灌注异常或意识恶化。应评整条链及趋势，不拿最好看的一个数字安慰自己。

00:07:29.472 --> 00:07:45.552
Hemostasis begins with local vascular responses and platelet adhesion/activation. Von Willebrand factor helps adhesion, while platelet mediators recruit more platelets. The first plug is strengthened by a fibrin network.
止血开始于局部血管反应及血小板黏附活化。血管性血友病因子帮助黏附，血小板介质再募集更多血小板，初步栓由纤维蛋白网加固。

00:07:45.552 --> 00:08:00.936
The traditional extrinsic and intrinsic teaching pathways converge toward thrombin generation. Thrombin converts fibrinogen to fibrin and factor thirteen stabilizes it. Calcium and appropriate cellular surfaces support the process.
传统外源及内源教学途径汇向产生凝血酶，后者把纤维蛋白原转为纤维蛋白，XIII再稳定；钙及适当细胞表面支持过程。

00:08:00.936 --> 00:08:15.912
Antiplatelets, anticoagulants and thrombolytics act at different parts of this chain. Aspirin is not a clot-dissolving drug. Do not infer stroke treatment or any new medicine permission from a general clotting diagram.
抗血小板、抗凝和溶栓药作用位置不同。阿司匹林不是溶解血块的药，不能从一般凝血图推卒中治疗或新增用药权限。

00:08:15.912 --> 00:08:30.168
For access and hemorrhage care, ask about anticoagulant and antiplatelet exposure and observe the actual bleeding. A route or fluid bag cannot replace bleeding control or the need to treat its cause.
血管通路及出血照护中，应问抗凝及抗血小板暴露，并看实际出血。通路或液袋不能替代止血和病因处理。

00:08:30.168 --> 00:08:45.912
ABO names red-cell surface antigens and corresponding plasma antibody patterns. RhD is another important antigen, but it is not the only clinically significant non-ABO feature. Exposure history can matter.
ABO描述红细胞表面抗原及相应血浆抗体模式，RhD是另一重要抗原，却不是唯一有临床意义的非ABO特征；暴露史也重要。

00:08:45.912 --> 00:08:58.608
The familiar O-negative donor shorthand concerns red-cell use under defined conditions. It is not a promise that any O-negative whole blood or plasma product is safe for everyone without further checks.
熟悉的O阴性供者简称，涉及特定条件下用红细胞，不能保证任意O阴性全血或血浆，不经其他核查就适合所有人。

00:08:58.608 --> 00:09:14.160
Laboratory typing, antibody screening and compatibility testing answer different questions. Patient and product identity remain essential even after a laboratory match. A classroom typing card is not the whole process.
化验定型、抗体筛查及相容检测回答不同问题。即使化验相合，患者和产品身份仍不可缺，课堂定型卡并非完整流程。

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:27.408
The assigned blood and line-care readings include this hospital knowledge so it is not omitted. They do not make transfusion an independent PCP action or turn crystalloid into an oxygen-carrying substitute.
指定血液及通路护理阅读含这部分医院知识，因此不会漏掉；但它不会让输血变PCP独立操作，也不会把晶体液变成携氧替代品。

00:09:27.408 --> 00:09:41.952
The heart wall has an inner lining, muscular middle and outer epicardial layer. The pericardial arrangement reduces friction and supports position; it can also constrain filling when abnormal pressure develops around the heart.
心壁有内衬、肌性中层和心外膜。心包结构减摩擦并支持定位；心周压力异常时，也会限制充盈。

00:09:41.952 --> 00:09:53.976
Valves open and close with pressure differences. Papillary muscles and chordae protect the AV leaflets against prolapse during contraction; they do not actively pull the leaflets open.
瓣随压差开闭。乳头肌及腱索防收缩时房室瓣叶翻入心房，不是主动拉开瓣叶。

00:09:53.976 --> 00:10:07.968
Coronary arteries supply the working muscle. Blood present inside a chamber does not automatically nourish the full thickness of its wall. Ischemia can therefore damage both electrical stability and pumping.
冠脉供应工作心肌。心腔里有血，不表示能自动营养整层心壁，因此缺血可同时损害电稳定与泵血。

00:10:07.968 --> 00:10:21.720
A normal-looking rhythm cannot exclude a coronary problem, valve failure or impaired filling. These structural and perfusion links explain why you continue examining the patient while recording electrical data.
节律看似正常，不能排除冠脉问题、瓣衰或充盈受损。所以记录电数据时，仍须继续检查患者。

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:34.920
During filling, atrial pressure exceeds ventricular pressure and the AV valves are open. Much filling is passive, followed by an atrial contribution. The pulmonary and aortic valves are closed.
充盈时心房压高于心室，房室瓣开放。大部分先被动充盈，随后有心房贡献，此时肺动脉及主动脉瓣关。

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:49.032
As ventricular contraction raises pressure above atrial pressure, AV valves close. For a brief phase all valves are shut, so pressure rises without volume leaving: isovolumetric contraction.
心室收缩使压力超过心房，房室瓣关闭。短暂阶段各瓣都关，压力升而容量未外流，叫等容收缩。

00:10:49.032 --> 00:11:05.616
When ventricular pressure exceeds outflow pressure, semilunar valves open and ejection follows. As pressure falls, they close. Both groups are again closed during early relaxation until ventricular pressure falls below atrial pressure.
心室压力超过流出道后，半月瓣开而射血；压力下降后又关。早期舒张两组再次都关，直到心室压低于心房。

00:11:05.616 --> 00:11:19.128
This sequence corrects the reversed valve sentence in the candidate MSN text. It also separates an electrical event from the later pressure and flow response, which is essential when interpreting an ECG.
这个顺序修正MSN候选正文中倒置的瓣膜句子，也把电事件与后续压力血流反应区分开，对解释ECG很重要。

00:11:19.128 --> 00:11:33.504
Normal activation starts in the SA region, spreads through atria and pauses in the AV region before rapid His-Purkinje distribution to ventricles. These are specialized cardiac cells, not simply a bundle of motor nerves.
正常激动起窦房区，传心房，在房室区延迟后，经希氏浦肯野快速分到心室。这是特化心脏细胞，不只是运动神经束。

00:11:33.504 --> 00:11:50.520
Pacemaker nodal cells and working ventricular cells have different action potentials. In the ventricular model, fast depolarization, a calcium-related plateau and potassium-related recovery do not have the same ionic timing as nodal automaticity.
结区起搏细胞与工作心室细胞动作电位不同。心室模型中的快速除极、钙相关平台及钾相关恢复，其离子时序不同于结区自律。

00:11:50.520 --> 00:12:05.592
Calcium triggers the contractile machinery, and the long refractory period helps prevent sustained contraction that would block refilling. Electrical activation is necessary for coordinated normal pumping but does not guarantee useful force.
钙触发收缩装置，长不应期帮助防止妨碍再充盈的持续收缩。正常协调泵血需要电激动，却不能保证产生有用力量。

00:12:05.592 --> 00:12:19.080
Ischemia, loading, structural damage or metabolic disturbance can interrupt the link. This is why a monitor waveform must be paired with a pulse/perfusion assessment, not used in place of it.
缺血、负荷、结构损伤或代谢紊乱可破坏这环连接，所以监护波形必须配脉搏灌注评估，不能取代它。

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:31.704
A twelve-lead ECG uses ten physical electrodes to derive twelve electrical views. A lead is not one catheter, one coronary artery or one direct measurement of blood flow.
12导联ECG用10个实体电极得到12个电视角。一个导联不是一根导管、一支冠脉，或一次直接血流测量。

00:12:31.704 --> 00:12:49.080
P represents atrial depolarization, QRS ventricular depolarization and T ventricular repolarization. The tiny SA-node discharge itself is not the surface P wave. Electrical timing and mechanical timing are related, not identical.
P代表心房除极，QRS为心室除极，T为心室复极。微小窦房结放电本身不是体表P波，电与机械时序相关但不同。

00:12:49.080 --> 00:13:04.368
Measure PR from P onset to QRS onset, not to the R peak. The original rhythm lesson works through calibration, rates, widths and relationships; the twelve-lead lesson adds correct acquisition and regional evidence.
PR从P起点到QRS起点，不到R峰。原创节律课示范校准、频率、宽度及关系，12导联课再加正确采集及区域证据。

00:13:04.368 --> 00:13:17.568
An organized rhythm without a pulse is an arrest problem, not a reassuring output. Conversely, a normal rhythm does not eliminate ACS or another cause of poor perfusion in the original patient.
有组织节律却无脉，是骤停问题，不是令人放心的心排。反过来，正常节律也不能排除原创患者的ACS或其他灌注差病因。

00:13:17.568 --> 00:13:46.464
The assigned conduction video connects several scales of physiology. Keep them separate. A nodal cell can depolarize spontaneously during phase four; the usual working ventricular cell has a relatively stable resting phase instead. Its rapid sodium-dependent upstroke is not the same as the nodal calcium-dependent upstroke. The corrected bilingual guide prevents the video’s simplified cell descriptions from becoming one universal action potential.
指定传导视频连接多个生理层级，但要分别理解。结区细胞第4期可自发去极，普通工作心室肌细胞则有较稳定静息期。后者依钠快速上升，不等于结区依钙的上升支。修正的中英指南，避免把视频简化细胞描述混成一种通用动作电位。

00:13:46.464 --> 00:14:16.728
The surface ECG summarizes electrical activity across tissue. It is not a direct recording of one cell or proof that a valve opened. Mechanical contraction follows activation, and pressure differences determine valve movement and forward flow. Heart sounds relate to valve closure rather than exact R or T peaks. Use the connected cycle lesson to explain filling, closed-valve pressure changes and ejection, then return to the patient’s actual perfusion.
体表ECG总结组织电活动，不是单个细胞直接记录，也不证明瓣膜已开。机械收缩跟随激动，压力差决定瓣膜运动及前向流。心音与瓣膜闭合相关，不是精确R峰或T峰。应连接周期课解释充盈、瓣膜闭合时压力变化及射血，再回到患者真实灌注。

00:14:16.728 --> 00:14:30.096
Stroke volume is the amount ejected in one beat and equals end-diastolic minus end-systolic volume. Cardiac output is that volume multiplied by beats per minute. Keep units visible until they cancel.
每搏量是一搏射出的量，等于舒张末容量减收缩末容量；心排量再乘每分钟搏数。单位应一直写到相消。

00:14:30.096 --> 00:14:42.672
In an original arithmetic example, eighty beats per minute times sixty-five millilitres per beat gives five thousand two hundred millilitres per minute, or five point two litres per minute.
原创算术例中，每分钟80次乘每搏65毫升，得每分钟5200毫升，即5.2升/分。

00:14:42.672 --> 00:14:54.384
If end-diastolic volume were one hundred thirty millilitres, that stroke volume would give an ejection fraction of fifty percent. The fraction and the minute output answer different questions.
若舒张末容量为130毫升，该每搏量对应射血分数50%。分数与每分钟输出回答不同问题。

00:14:54.384 --> 00:15:07.032
Neither the ECG nor the cuff supplied the assumed volume. Do not report calculated example output as if it were measured in this patient, and do not infer adequate perfusion from a fraction alone.
ECG及袖带均未提供这个假设容量。不能把例题计算说成已测患者心排，也不能只凭分数推充分灌注。

00:15:07.032 --> 00:15:20.448
Preload concerns filling-related stretch before contraction. Contractility concerns the muscle force-generating state under comparable loading. Afterload is the load the ventricle must overcome to eject.
前负荷涉及收缩前充盈相关伸展，收缩性涉及可比负荷下的产力状态，后负荷是心室射血需克服的负荷。

00:15:20.448 --> 00:15:33.408
Within physiological limits, increased filling can increase stroke volume through the Frank-Starling mechanism. That does not mean increasing preload is identical to an independent increase in contractility.
生理范围内，增加充盈可通过Frank-Starling机制增加每搏量，但不能说增前负荷等于独立增强收缩性。

00:15:33.408 --> 00:15:48.624
In a poorly functioning or stiff ventricle, added volume can increase filling pressure and lung congestion without much useful output. A small pressure rise during fluid is not proof that every consequence is beneficial.
功能差或僵硬心室中，加量可升充盈压和肺淤血，却没增加多少有用心排。补液时血压稍升，不能证明全部后果有益。

00:15:48.624 --> 00:16:02.112
For the original patient, ask about cardiac and renal history, current breathing and the cause of low pressure. Connect any authorized fluid trial to a specific benefit and an early reassessment point.
对原创患者要问心肾史，查当前呼吸和低压原因。任何获准液体试验都应连具体益处及早期复评点。

00:16:02.112 --> 00:16:14.400
Blood moves because there is a pressure gradient. The relevant quantity is a difference between upstream and downstream pressures, not an isolated pressure number with no reference to the rest of the circuit.
血移动因有压差。关键是上下游压力差，不是脱离其余回路的孤立压力数字。

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:26.736
In the simplified model, flow equals pressure difference divided by resistance. If downstream venous pressure rises while upstream pressure is unchanged, the driving gradient can fall.
简化模型中，流量等于压差除阻力。上游不变、下游静脉压升时，推动梯度可能下降。

00:16:26.736 --> 00:16:40.176
Arteriolar caliber strongly influences resistance and distribution. Venous capacitance and return influence filling. The same cuff pressure can therefore accompany different output and regional flow states.
小动脉口径强烈影响阻力和分配，静脉容量及回流影响充盈。因此相同袖带压力，可能伴不同心排和区域血流。

00:16:40.176 --> 00:16:53.640
Use pressure as evidence alongside awareness, skin/perfusion, pulse and breathing. Do not call shock absent merely because compensation has kept the pressure above a remembered threshold.
血压要与意识、皮肤灌注、脉搏和呼吸合用。不能因代偿使血压仍高于记忆阈值，就说没有休克。

00:16:53.640 --> 00:17:09.192
Poiseuille describes ideal laminar flow through a rigid tube. Resistance rises with length and viscosity and falls with the fourth power of radius. Radius is especially influential because it is raised to that fourth power.
Poiseuille描述刚性管内理想层流。阻力随长度和黏度增，随半径四次方减，四次方使半径尤其重要。

00:17:09.192 --> 00:17:21.336
Halving radius gives one half to the fourth power, or one-sixteenth. Resistance becomes sixteen times higher, and at the same pressure gradient the ideal flow becomes one-sixteenth.
半径减半，二分之一的四次方是十六分之一，因此阻力成16倍，同压差下理想流量为十六分之一。

00:17:21.336 --> 00:17:34.272
The lesson supports understanding vessel constriction and the importance of access-device geometry. It does not prove every clinical catheter or living vessel will change flow by precisely that amount.
这帮助理解血管收缩及通路几何为何重要，却不证明每根临床导管或活体血管都精确按同一倍数变化。

00:17:34.272 --> 00:17:48.120
For a line problem, inspect the actual route, kink, valve, site and device instructions. Raising pressure to overcome unexplained resistance is not a safe substitute for finding its cause.
通路出问题时应查实际路线、弯折、阀、局部及器材说明。提高压力硬顶未知阻力，不能安全替代查原因。

00:17:48.120 --> 00:18:05.448
Most body water is intracellular, while extracellular fluid includes plasma, interstitial and smaller transcellular spaces. A common adult model places about two-thirds inside cells and one-third outside, with substantial individual variation.
大部分体水在细胞内，细胞外包括血浆、组织间及较小跨细胞空间。常用成人模型约三分之二在内、三分之一在外，但个体变化相当大。

00:18:05.448 --> 00:18:18.648
Ask three different questions: how much fluid is present, where is it, and how concentrated are the effective solutes? A patient can have excess tissue fluid yet poor effective circulation.
要分三问：总量多少，位于哪里，有效溶质多浓？组织液过多者，仍可有效循环差。

00:18:18.648 --> 00:18:32.376
Dehydration, hypovolemia and hyponatremia are therefore not interchangeable. They concern water deficit, circulating volume and a concentration respectively, although combinations can occur.
因此脱水、低血容量及低钠不能互换；分别涉及缺水、循环量和浓度，当然也可组合出现。

00:18:32.376 --> 00:18:45.312
The diagram is an illustrative compartment model, not a measured forty-two-litre patient or a formula for choosing bolus size. Real fluid distribution changes with disease, barriers and treatment.
图是区室示例，不是测得患者有42升水，也不是选补液量公式。真实分布随疾病、屏障和治疗变。

00:18:45.312 --> 00:19:00.792
Osmosis describes net water movement across a selectively permeable membrane toward the side with more effective solute. The candidate FON paragraph gives contradictory directions; keep this correct relationship rather than learning both.
渗透描述水跨选择通透膜，净移向有效溶质更多一侧。FON候选段两句方向矛盾，应采用正确关系，不两句都背。

00:19:00.792 --> 00:19:14.496
Tonicity concerns the effect of effective solutes on cell volume. It is related to but not identical to total measured osmolality, because not every particle remains an effective barrier-separated solute.
张力涉及有效溶质对细胞体积的影响，与总测得渗透浓度相关但不同，因为不是每种颗粒都持续被膜隔开而产生有效作用。

00:19:14.496 --> 00:19:31.872
Relatively isotonic crystalloid expands extracellular fluid; it does not all remain in plasma. Hypotonic fluid can move water into cells, while hypertonic fluid can draw it out. Dextrose handling changes the later behavior of some solutions.
相对等张晶体液扩细胞外液，不全留血浆；低张液可使水入细胞，高张液可使水出细胞。一些含糖液的后续行为还受糖处理改变。

00:19:31.872 --> 00:19:46.296
This prediction is not a one-number prescribing table. Actual illness, sodium acuity, circulation, product, permitted indication and monitoring determine the treatment plan, not the word isotonic alone.
方向预测不是只凭一个数选药的表。治疗需看病情、钠变化急慢、循环、产品、获准指征和监测，不由“等张”两字决定。

00:19:46.296 --> 00:20:31.920
Trace the source capillary-bed diagram as a branching route: terminal arteriole, metarteriole, exchange capillaries and postcapillary venule. Its precapillary sphincters regulate entry into branches; its thoroughfare channel continues toward the venule, while an arteriovenous anastomosis is a direct bypass. Changing local resistance can redistribute flow without changing the amount of hemoglobin in the blood. Vasomotion means changing microvascular flow/tone, not the ECG rhythm or a palpable pulse count. This is a schematic teaching arrangement, not proof that every organ has identical sphincters or that all resting muscle and digestive microvessels are closed.
按分支路线追来源毛细血管床图：终末小动脉、后微动脉、交换毛细血管，再到毛细血管后微静脉。图中毛细血管前括约肌调分支入口，直捷通道通向微静脉，动静脉吻合则直接旁路。局部阻力改变可重新分配血流，而不改变血中血红蛋白量。血管舒缩性运动是微血流及张力变化，不是ECG心律或可摸脉的计数。这是教学示意结构，不证明所有器官都有相同括约肌，也不表示休息时肌肉及消化系统微血管全部关闭。

00:20:31.920 --> 00:21:19.416
Complete the assigned capillary-exchange example with its return route. In the source classic daily-volume model, 24 L filtered minus 20.4 L reabsorbed leaves 3.6 L for lymphatic return. The arithmetic is a balance within that model, not a fixed daily loss or an IV-fluid order. Lymphatic capillaries collect excess interstitial fluid and proteins; larger lymphatic pathways return them to the venous circulation. Obstruction or overwhelmed drainage can therefore contribute to edema. Keep this alongside the modern barrier/steady-state qualification already taught, rather than treating the source venous-end reabsorption drawing as a universal account of every tissue.
把指定毛细血管交换例连到回流路线。来源经典日容量模型中，滤出24L减再吸收20.4L，剩3.6L需由淋巴回流。这是在模型内做平衡，不是固定每日丢失量或静脉补液医嘱。淋巴毛细管收集多余间质液和蛋白，经较大淋巴通路回到静脉循环；阻塞或回流负担过大因此可促水肿。应与已有的现代屏障及稳态局限讲解一起学，不能把来源静脉端再吸收图当所有组织的普遍完整机制。

00:21:19.416 --> 00:21:34.896
Oxygen and carbon dioxide mainly cross by diffusion down their gradients. Bulk fluid movement through a microvascular barrier is a different process. Calling all nutrient and gas exchange filtration hides that distinction.
氧和二氧化碳主要沿梯度扩散，液体整体跨微血管屏障是另一过程。把所有气体营养交换都称滤过，会掩盖区别。

00:21:34.896 --> 00:21:48.960
Hydrostatic pressure concerns fluid pressure against a boundary. Oncotic pressure is the protein-related osmotic contribution. Both sides of the barrier matter, along with permeability and lymphatic drainage.
静水压涉及液体对边界的压力，胶体渗透压是蛋白相关渗透贡献。屏障两侧、通透性及淋巴引流都重要。

00:21:48.960 --> 00:22:02.016
Higher capillary pressure can favor outward fluid movement. Reduced effective plasma-protein restraint, increased permeability or blocked lymph drainage can also promote interstitial accumulation.
毛细血管压力较高，可利向外移动；有效血浆蛋白约束减少、通透性增加或淋巴阻塞，也可促进间质积液。

00:22:02.016 --> 00:22:13.896
This explains why ankle edema has several possible mechanisms and cannot tell you, by itself, that the patient has enough effective circulating volume or should receive a particular fluid.
所以踝水肿有多种机制，不能独自证明有效循环量足够，也不能决定该给什么液体。

00:22:13.896 --> 00:22:30.192
The classic four-force model compares capillary and interstitial hydrostatic pressures with the opposing protein osmotic contributions. A positive outward driving result favors filtration in that model; a negative result favors inward movement.
经典四力模型比较毛细血管及间质静水压，以及相反的蛋白渗透贡献。该模型中，向外驱动结果为正利滤出，为负利向内。

00:22:30.192 --> 00:22:45.768
The candidate simplifies interstitial terms to zero. At its arterial example, thirty-five minus twenty-five gives positive ten millimetres of mercury. At its venous example, eighteen minus twenty-five gives negative seven.
候选把间质项设零。其动脉端例35减25得正10毫米汞柱，静脉端例18减25得负7。

00:22:45.768 --> 00:22:59.520
Be able to explain the sign, the assumed forces and the arithmetic. These are teaching values, not measured pressures in the original patient. A diagram of forces is not a quantity of fluid to administer.
应能解释符号、假设的力和算术。这些是教学值，不是原创患者实测压，力图也不是应该给多少液体。

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:12.072
Now add the model boundary on the next slide. Learning the classic examination explanation does not require pretending that every real venous capillary continuously absorbs fluid exactly this way.
下一页加入模型边界。会解释经典考试模型，不需要假装每条真实静脉端毛细血管都持续精确如此吸液。

00:23:12.072 --> 00:23:26.304
Microvascular research shows that the endothelial glycocalyx and the fluid immediately beneath it matter to the effective barrier. Whole-interstitial protein concentration alone does not fully determine that local gradient.
微血管研究说明，内皮糖萼及其正下方液体，影响有效屏障；整个间质的蛋白浓度，不能完整决定这个局部梯度。

00:23:26.304 --> 00:23:39.888
Many tissues maintain slight outward filtration at steady state rather than continuous venous-end reabsorption. Transient absorption and specialized organs are important exceptions to a simple absolute rule.
许多组织稳态下仍轻度外滤，不是静脉端持续再吸收。短暂吸收及特化器官又提示不能换成另一条绝对规则。

00:23:39.888 --> 00:23:53.136
For this week, retain the force directions and explain the classic school calculation, but also name permeability, local barrier conditions and lymphatic return. These make the picture more complete.
本周既要保留力方向、会讲学校经典计算，也应指出通透性、局部屏障及淋巴回流，让图景更完整。

00:23:53.136 --> 00:24:05.496
Do not turn this into an albumin or fluid prescription. Neither the classic drawing nor its revision says that adding a product will reliably pull all established edema back into the circulation.
不要把它变成白蛋白或液体处方。经典图及修正模型都没说，加入某产品就能把既有水肿可靠拉回血管。

00:24:05.496 --> 00:24:20.280
ADH is made in the hypothalamus and released from the posterior pituitary, then acts on the kidneys to retain water. The kidneys do not produce ADH in response to tubule pressure, despite that candidate FON sentence.
ADH在下丘脑合成、经垂体后叶释放，再作用肾保水。肾不会按小管压力产生ADH，FON候选那句需修正。

00:24:20.280 --> 00:24:35.976
RAAS links renal sensing and renin with angiotensin signaling, vascular effects and adrenal-cortical aldosterone. Aldosterone promotes renal sodium retention and potassium excretion; water balance also depends on other signals.
RAAS把肾感知、肾素、血管紧张素信号、血管效应及皮质醛固酮连起来。醛固酮促肾潴钠排钾，水调节还依其他信号。

00:24:35.976 --> 00:24:51.168
Cardiac stretch-related natriuretic peptides favor sodium and water excretion and oppose some retaining responses. Local metabolic and myogenic mechanisms distribute flow, but all mechanisms operate within limits.
心脏牵张相关利钠肽有利排钠水，对抗部分潴留反应；局部代谢及肌源机制分配血流，但所有机制都有极限。

00:24:51.168 --> 00:25:06.552
In acute illness, a compensatory response may preserve one number while another link fails. You still need serial observations, cause assessment and a controlled treatment plan rather than faith that homeostasis will fix everything.
急病中，某代偿可保一个数字，而别的环已失败。仍需连续观察、病因评估及受控方案，不能相信稳态会自动修好一切。

00:25:06.552 --> 00:25:21.648
Potassium is predominantly inside cells. Serum concentration changes with body stores, renal handling and movement between cells and extracellular fluid. Medicines, insulin and acid-base problems can contribute.
钾主要在细胞内。血清浓度随总储备、肾处理及细胞内外转移变；药物、胰岛素及酸碱问题均可影响。

00:25:21.648 --> 00:25:36.216
High or low potassium can affect muscle and cardiac electrical function. A concerning ECG supports urgent assessment, but normal or nonclassic waveforms cannot reliably exclude a dangerous potassium disorder.
高低钾都可影响肌肉和心电功能。可疑ECG支持紧急评估，但正常或不典型波形，不能可靠排除危险钾异常。

00:25:36.216 --> 00:25:49.344
Do not estimate the potassium level or choose replacement from a T wave. Severe hyperkalemia management has distinct protection, shift and removal purposes under the actual current pathway.
不能从T波估钾值或选补钾。重度高钾处理在现行路径下，有保护、转移及去除等不同目的。

00:25:49.344 --> 00:26:03.288
The hospital replacement boxes are assigned knowledge, not a PCP potassium order. Undiluted rapid IV potassium can be fatal, and a generic textbook rate is not a universal safe maximum.
医院补充框是指定知识，不是PCP补钾医嘱。未稀释快速静脉钾可致命，通用教材速度也不是普遍安全上限。

00:26:03.288 --> 00:26:15.264
Serum sodium is not simply dietary salt or a direct measure of circulating volume. It concerns sodium relative to water, with important effects on cell water and brain function.
血钠不只是吃盐多少，也不是直接循环量计。它涉及钠相对水的关系，重要地影响细胞水及脑功能。

00:26:15.264 --> 00:26:29.184
Low and high sodium can have serious neurological consequences, and the speed of change matters. The diagnosis, cause and controlled correction plan cannot be guessed from thirst or one pressure reading.
低高钠都可有严重神经后果，变化速度也重要；不能从口渴或一次血压猜诊断、病因和纠正方案。

00:26:29.184 --> 00:26:42.096
Calcium supports signaling, contraction and coagulation. Total calcium and ionized calcium are not the same result, and albumin-related effects can alter interpretation of a total value.
钙支持信号、收缩及凝血。总钙与离子钙不是同一结果，白蛋白相关影响也可改变总值解释。

00:26:42.096 --> 00:26:54.048
For every laboratory claim, keep the analyte and units attached. A result in milligrams per decilitre cannot simply be compared with a remembered ionized value in millimoles per litre.
每个化验判断都应保留项目和单位。mg/dL结果不能直接与记忆中的离子钙mmol/L值比较。

00:26:54.048 --> 00:27:10.944
Magnesium supports neuromuscular and cardiac function. Losses, medicines and poor intake can contribute to deficiency; renal impairment or magnesium-containing products can cause excess. Neither direction is diagnosed from a symptom list alone.
镁支持神经肌肉及心脏功能。丢失、药物及摄入少可致缺乏，肾受损或含镁产品可致过多；两个方向都不能仅按症状表确诊。

00:27:10.944 --> 00:27:26.544
Chloride is linked to extracellular salt/water and acid-base processes. Vomiting can lose chloride-rich gastric fluid. Interpret the cause and full pattern rather than inventing a distinct symptom for every chloride value.
氯联系细胞外盐水及酸碱，呕吐会丢富氯胃液。应看病因和完整模式，不能给每个氯值编一种独特症状。

00:27:26.544 --> 00:27:42.024
Bicarbonate is an important buffer, related to carbon dioxide elimination and renal regulation. A low result is not automatic permission to give bicarbonate. Respiratory rate alone cannot provide the full blood-gas diagnosis.
碳酸氢根是重要缓冲成分，联系排二氧化碳及肾调节。低值不是自动给碳酸氢钠的许可，只靠呼吸次数也不能得到完整血气诊断。

00:27:42.024 --> 00:27:58.416
Phosphate contributes to energy transfer, membranes and bone. Kidney function, nutrition and shifts during treatment affect it. Keep correct units and actual laboratory intervals; the candidate PHARM phosphate-unit error is identified in its guide.
磷酸盐参与能量转移、膜和骨，肾、营养及治疗中转移会影响它。须保正确单位和真实参考范围，PHARM候选单位错误在导读中单独标明。

00:27:58.416 --> 00:28:11.256
Return to the original patient. Ask how much intake was possible, how long vomiting continued, whether diarrhea or bleeding occurred and what medicines or chronic disease could affect losses and compensation.
回到原创患者：问能摄入多少、呕吐持续多久、有无腹泻或出血，以及药物和慢病如何影响丢失及代偿。

00:28:11.256 --> 00:28:25.800
Look for a coherent pattern across awareness, pulse, pressure, capillary/skin findings and breathing. Dry mouth or poor skin turgor is not a precise fluid-deficit measurement, especially across ages.
应寻找意识、脉搏、血压、再充盈皮肤及呼吸的连贯模式。口干或皮弹差不是精确缺液测量，跨年龄时更如此。

00:28:25.800 --> 00:28:39.864
Intake/output records, weights and laboratory trends can help when actually available and reliable. A fixed urine-per-hour value is not an endpoint you must wait to measure before recognizing acute deterioration.
出入量、体重和化验趋势真实可用且可靠时能帮忙，但不能为了等测固定每小时尿量，才承认急性恶化。

00:28:39.864 --> 00:28:53.352
Say what else could explain the presentation and what evidence would change the plan. This improves reasoning without delaying treatment of immediate airway, breathing, circulation or catastrophic bleeding threats.
说出还有什么能解释、什么证据会改方案。这能改善推理，却不能延误即时气道、呼吸、循环或灾难出血处理。

00:28:53.352 --> 00:29:06.864
Now add a history of heart and kidney disease and increasing ankle swelling. The patient may have excessive tissue fluid while effective organ circulation is poor. These observations are not mutually exclusive.
现在加上心肾病和踝肿增加。患者可组织液多，同时有效器官循环差，这两种所见并不互斥。

00:29:06.864 --> 00:29:23.160
Check current breathing effort, lung findings, saturation quality, perfusion and change over time. An absence of one classic sign does not settle the mechanism, and low pressure is not an automatic instruction for an unrestricted fluid load.
查呼吸用力、肺所见、饱和度质量、灌注及时间变化。少一个典型征不定机制，低压也不等于无限补液指令。

00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:38.664
The hospital reading discusses restriction, diuretics and dialysis as selected treatments. It does not authorize independent PCP initiation of those therapies or a universal compression/elevation response to acute dyspnea.
医院阅读讨论限水、利尿及透析等选择性治疗，不授权PCP自行开始，也不支持急性气促时一律加压或抬腿。

00:29:38.664 --> 00:29:50.712
This is why a fluid intervention needs a purpose and repeated benefit/harm checks. The next step must fit the cause and actual authority, not simply the easiest available bag.
所以液体干预要有目的并反复查益处及伤害。下一步应适合病因和实际权限，不是用最顺手的一袋。

00:29:50.712 --> 00:30:04.128
First state which current care need justifies vascular treatment. An access route is a means, not the objective. Consent and technical convenience do not by themselves create a clinical indication.
先说明当前哪项照护需要支持血管治疗。通路是手段，不是目标；同意和技术方便都不能单独创造临床指征。

00:30:04.128 --> 00:30:18.312
Then verify the actual product, concentration, route, compatibility and authorized amount/rate. Infusion arithmetic answers delivery questions only after the clinical plan and source are correct.
再核实际产品、浓度、途径、相容性及获准量速。只有临床方案和来源正确后，输液算术才回答如何给。

00:30:18.312 --> 00:30:33.792
Name what should improve and when you will check it. For a perfusion-directed intervention, that may involve awareness, pulse/pressure and skin/perfusion alongside breathing, rather than pursuing one isolated number.
说预期何物改善、何时查。以灌注为目的时，可看意识、脉搏血压、皮肤灌注并兼顾呼吸，不只是追一个数字。

00:30:33.792 --> 00:30:47.928
Also name stop or escalation findings: new breathing difficulty, local pain/swelling, wrong product or unexpected worsening. A completed calculation is not permission to ignore new evidence.
也需说明停止或升级征象：新呼吸困难、局部痛肿、产品不对或意外恶化。算对不能成为忽略新证据的许可。

00:30:47.928 --> 00:31:00.912
During an authorized simulation infusion, pressure rises slightly, but the patient becomes more breathless and has new crackles and access-site discomfort. The pump still displays the planned setting.
获准模拟输注中，血压略升，但患者更气促，出现新湿啰音及穿刺处不适；泵仍显示原设定。

00:31:00.912 --> 00:31:14.016
This is not uncomplicated success. A correct setting does not prove the right fluid reached a safe site or that its physiological effect was helpful. Local and systemic problems may coexist.
这不是无并发症成功。设定对，不证明正确液体经安全部位进入，也不证明生理作用有益；局部和全身问题可同时存在。

00:31:14.016 --> 00:31:30.840
Stop implicated delivery as appropriate and reassess ABCs, perfusion, the limb and the entire administration path. Do not force-flush a painful swollen site, and do not let one local explanation account for all breathing deterioration.
应视情况停相关给入，重评ABC、灌注、肢体及整条输注路径。不能强冲痛肿部位，也不能让一个局部解释包办所有呼吸恶化。

00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:42.576
Escalate with the actual product, amount, timing, baseline and change. The school questions are concrete here: what changed, what should have changed and what got worse?
升级沟通时应报真实产品、量、时间、基线和变化。学校三问在此很具体：变了什么，原应怎样变，什么更糟？

00:31:42.576 --> 00:31:56.328
Reliable pressure needs correct cuff selection and placement, a supported limb near heart level and the appropriate measurement method. A monitor cannot rescue a poorly sized cuff or repeated movement artifact.
可靠血压需选放正确袖带、支持肢体近心脏水平，并用合适方法。监护仪救不了尺寸不对或反复移动伪差。

00:31:56.328 --> 00:32:09.912
The assigned two-step method first estimates systolic pressure by palpation, then obtains the auscultatory measurement with a suitable reinflation target. This reduces the risk of missing an auscultatory gap.
指定两步法先触诊估收缩压，再以适当再充气目标作听诊测量，减少漏过听诊间隙风险。

00:32:09.912 --> 00:32:25.680
For the original value one hundred fourteen over seventy-two, pulse pressure is forty-two. At an ordinary rate, diastolic plus one-third pulse pressure estimates mean pressure as eighty-six, not the simple average of the two numbers.
原创114/72的脉压为42。一般心率下，用舒张压加脉压三分之一，估平均压86，不是把两个数简单平均。

00:32:25.680 --> 00:32:38.160
Record method and conditions, then compare the patient. An improving cuff value with worsening awareness or breathing must trigger more reasoning, not be selected as the only outcome that counts.
记录方法条件后再比较患者。袖带数改善但意识或呼吸恶化，应引发进一步推理，不能只挑改善数字作唯一结局。

00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:51.120
Before the first planned intervention, say what else could explain the presentation and identify one useful discriminating observation. This should be brief and must not delay an immediate lifesaving action.
首个计划干预前，说出另一个可能解释及一个有区分作用的观察。应简短，不能延误立即救命动作。

00:32:51.120 --> 00:33:07.200
For the vomiting patient, simple volume loss is plausible, but occult bleeding, infection, medication effects or pump dysfunction may alter the plan. Do not list every disease; select a credible alternative and explain why it matters.
呕吐患者虽可简单失液，隐匿出血、感染、药物或泵受损仍可改变方案。不是列完所有病，而是选可信替代解释并说为何重要。

00:33:07.200 --> 00:33:19.296
After an intervention, compare intended and actual change, then search for harm. A device number is only one part of the route check; the physiological response is another.
干预后比较预期与实际变化，再找伤害。器材数字只是通路核查一部分，生理反应是另一部分。

00:33:19.296 --> 00:33:34.248
The mental-health judgment reading supplies a disciplined recognize, analyze, prioritize, act and evaluate process. Use it without diagnostic overshadowing or assuming that calm behavior proves normal circulation.
精神健康判断阅读提供有纪律的识别、分析、排序、行动及评价过程。应用时不能让既有标签遮蔽新病，也不能因安静就认为循环正常。

00:33:34.248 --> 00:33:49.632
The A&P guide includes the regional arterial and venous pathways, not only the small set useful for inserting a line. Trace upper-limb return through axillary, subclavian and brachiocephalic veins to the superior vena cava.
A&P导读包含区域动静脉路线，不只挑置管有用的小部分。应能从上肢经腋、锁骨下和头臂静脉追到上腔。

00:33:49.632 --> 00:34:05.544
The hepatic portal system places digestive or splenic exchange before liver sinusoids and systemic return. This is one foundation for understanding why many enteral substances encounter hepatic processing before the wider circulation.
肝门系统把消化或脾的交换放在肝血窦及体回流之前，有助理解许多肠内物质为何先遇肝处理，再进更广循环。

00:34:05.544 --> 00:34:22.464
Fetal circulation uses placental exchange and three major shunts: ductus venosus, foramen ovale and ductus arteriosus. One umbilical vein returns relatively oxygen-rich placental blood and two arteries go toward the placenta.
胎儿靠胎盘交换，并有静脉导管、卵圆孔和动脉导管三大分流。一根脐静脉带回相对富氧胎盘血，两根动脉走向胎盘。

00:34:22.464 --> 00:34:40.344
Birth changes pulmonary resistance, oxygen and pressure relationships. Functional closure and anatomical closure are not the same moment. Use the paired guide to explain each connection and remnant rather than assuming a newborn has a smaller copy of the adult circuit.
出生改变肺阻力、氧及压差，功能和解剖关闭不是同一瞬间。对照导读解释各连接及残迹，不能把新生儿当较小成人回路。

00:34:40.344 --> 00:35:31.224
Use the assigned FON Table 20.1 as a named source reference, not a universal laboratory standard. Its adult intervals are sodium 135-145 mEq/L, potassium 3.5-5.1 mEq/L, chloride 96-106 mEq/L and bicarbonate 22-29 mEq/L. It gives total calcium 8.6-10.2 mg/dL, magnesium 1.5-2.4 mEq/L and phosphate 3.4-4.5 mg/dL. Keep each number attached to its analyte and unit. A different laboratory interval does not automatically mean the patient or laboratory is wrong.
把指定FON表20.1当作具名来源参考，不是所有化验室统一标准。其成人区间是钠135至145mEq/L、钾3.5至5.1mEq/L、氯96至106mEq/L、碳酸氢根22至29mEq/L；总钙8.6至10.2mg/dL、镁1.5至2.4mEq/L、磷酸盐3.4至4.5mg/dL。每个数都要带项目及单位。另一化验室区间不同，不自动表示患者或化验室错误。

00:35:31.224 --> 00:36:12.168
For the singly charged sodium and potassium ions, the numerical values in mEq/L and mmol/L are equal; for a divalent ion such as magnesium, they are not. Milligrams measure mass, not the same quantity as millimoles or milliequivalents. Total calcium is not ionized calcium. Symptoms overlap: both sodium directions can disturb awareness or cause seizures, while potassium disturbances may affect weakness and cardiac conduction. Check the actual result and clinical situation rather than diagnosing a serum level from a nonspecific symptom or ordering replacement from this reference table.
单价钠钾的mEq/L与mmol/L数值相等；镁等二价离子则不相等。毫克计质量，不与毫摩尔或毫当量表示相同数量。总钙不等于离子钙。症状可重叠：高低钠均可扰乱意识或致抽搐，钾紊乱可影响肌力与心脏传导。须核实际结果及临床情况，不能凭非特异症状推血值，也不能按参考表自行开补充方案。

00:36:12.168 --> 00:36:51.000
Separate the source breathing table from a treatment instruction. Hyperventilation means alveolar ventilation is excessive relative to carbon-dioxide production, not simply that the respiratory rate is high. FON Table 19.1 labels slower or faster breathing as compensation for primary respiratory disorders; that is an oversimplification. Buffering and renal bicarbonate adjustment are important compensating processes, whereas reversing the abnormal ventilation addresses the respiratory cause. Do not deliberately suppress needed breathing or wait for a tired patient to normalize spontaneously.
须把来源呼吸表与治疗指令分开。过度通气指肺泡通气相对二氧化碳生成过多，不只是呼吸次数快。FON表19.1把变慢或变快的呼吸列为原发呼吸紊乱的代偿，过于简化。缓冲及肾对碳酸氢根的调整是重要代偿过程；纠正异常通气则是在处理呼吸病因。不能故意抑制必要呼吸，也不能等待疲劳患者自行恢复正常。

00:36:51.000 --> 00:37:30.144
Read the membrane picture by mechanism, not the shape of the illustrated particle. Small nonpolar gases can cross the lipid bilayer by simple diffusion; glucose commonly needs a carrier, and ions require suitable channels or transporters. Facilitated diffusion remains passive, while pumps and coupled transport use energy directly or indirectly. The FON paragraph that groups glucose, proteins and electrolytes as freely crossing a semipermeable membrane is too broad. Water movement, solute movement and active maintenance of a gradient are three different questions.
膜图要按机制读，不按粒子画成什么形状猜。小而非极性的气体可经脂双层简单扩散，葡萄糖通常需载体，离子需适当通道或转运体。易化扩散仍是被动过程，泵及耦联转运则直接或间接用能。FON把葡萄糖、蛋白及电解质并列成能自由通过半透膜，范围过宽。水怎样移动、溶质怎样移动、梯度怎样被主动维持，是三个不同问题。

00:37:30.144 --> 00:38:07.560
The Buerger-disease box describes a different vascular problem from ordinary plaque disease: thromboangiitis obliterans can obstruct vessels in the extremities, producing ischemic pain, ulcers and tissue loss, and is strongly associated with tobacco exposure. Learn the disease name and perfusion mechanism without diagnosing it from smoking alone. The social-learning point is dependence, barriers and practical support, not blaming the person or treating gender, ethnicity or income as a diagnosis. A new painful or poorly perfused limb still needs prompt clinical assessment.
Buerger病框描述的血管问题不同于普通斑块病：血栓闭塞性脉管炎可阻塞肢体血管，造成缺血痛、溃疡及组织损失，并与烟草暴露强相关。要认病名及灌注机制，不能仅凭吸烟诊断。社会学习重点是依赖、障碍及实际支持，不是责备患者，也不是把性别、族群或收入当诊断。新出现疼痛或灌注不良的肢体仍需及时临床评估。

00:38:07.560 --> 00:38:49.896
Read advanced hemodynamics with its denominator. The source Table 19.2 lists cardiac output about 4-8 L/min and cardiac index about 2.5-4 L/min/m2 as adult reference examples; cardiac index is output divided by body surface area. For an original assumed output of 4.2 L/min and surface area of 1.8 m2, the index is about 2.33 L/min/m2. The arithmetic does not measure an actual patient or establish the cause of poor perfusion. Neither a normal fraction nor a population output range replaces serial assessment.
高级血流动力学也要看分母。来源表19.2把成人心排量约4至8L/min、心脏指数约2.5至4L/min/m2列为参考例；心脏指数是心排量除体表面积。原创假设心排量4.2L/min、体表面积1.8m2，指数约2.33L/min/m2。这道算术并未测量真实患者，也未确定灌注差的原因。正常分数或人群心排范围都不能替代连续评估。

00:38:49.896 --> 00:39:32.280
Read Table 10.4 with its actual examples: 0.9 percent sodium chloride and lactated Ringer solution are the relatively isotonic examples, 0.45 percent sodium chloride is hypotonic, and 3 or 5 percent sodium chloride are hypertonic. The accompanying red-cell picture illustrates cell-volume response, not the percentage of an infused bag that remains inside a vein. Its sodium-based treatment columns and blanket renal-failure contraindication are not a universal emergency fluid-selection rule. Use the actual diagnosis, product and authorized pathway; an isotonic label does not prevent overload.
表10.4须连实际例子读：0.9%氯化钠及乳酸林格液是相对等张例，0.45%氯化钠为低张，3%或5%氯化钠为高张。配套红细胞图说明细胞体积反应，不是输进一袋后有多少百分比留在静脉内。其按血钠分类的治疗栏及笼统肾衰禁忌，不是通用急症选液规则。应依真实诊断、产品及授权路径；标签写等张也不能防止容量过多。

00:39:32.280 --> 00:40:17.448
Keep the assigned ECG table separate from a diagnostic shortcut. It lists P duration 0.06-0.12 seconds, PR 0.12-0.20, QRS 0.06-0.10 and a raw QT example 0.36-0.44. Measure complete onset-to-end boundaries at the actual paper speed. The school rhythm method treats QRS at least 0.12 seconds as wide; do not wait for it to exceed 0.12 because of the source table wording. QT depends on rate, and a nominal table interval cannot replace appropriate correction or the clinical ECG interpretation.
须把指定ECG表与诊断捷径分开。它列P时限0.06至0.12秒、PR 0.12至0.20秒、QRS 0.06至0.10秒，以及原始QT例0.36至0.44秒。要按真实走纸速度量完整起止。学校节律方法把QRS至少0.12秒视为宽，不能因来源表用词而等到超过0.12才认宽。QT依心率变化，表中名义区间不能替代适当校正及临床ECG解释。

00:40:17.448 --> 00:40:57.912
A flutter ratio describes conduction, not a second heart rate to add. In an original assumed atrial rate of 300/min with fixed 4:1 conduction, ventricular rate is 75/min. Count atrial activity and QRS separately, including waves hidden in a complex; do not infer a ratio from a caption alone. The source uses SVT both as a broad above-ventricle category and beside a regular narrow-complex drawing. State the observed regularity, QRS width and atrial evidence instead of assuming all SVT means the same mechanism or all flutter is a ventricular tachycardia.
房扑比例描述传导，不是另一个需要相加的心率。原创假设房率300/min且固定4:1传导，室率为75/min。须分别数房性活动及QRS，并考虑藏在复合波内的房波，不能只凭图注推比例。来源把SVT既作室上性的大类，也放在规则窄波示意图旁。应说清所见规则性、QRS宽及房性证据，而不认定所有SVT都是同一机制，或所有房扑都为心室心动过速。

00:40:57.912 --> 00:41:39.336
The final assigned page describes a hospital arrest team: airway/ventilation, leadership and treatment decisions, compressions/medicines/recording, pharmacy checks and support for loved ones. Transfer the teamwork principles, not the assumption that every prehospital crew has each profession present. Assign roles, communicate doses and actions with closed-loop confirmation, preserve compression quality and record timing. Keep patient/family communication and handover in the plan. This is a team rehearsal framework, not a new drug, pacing or independent hospital-role authorization.
指定末页描述医院复苏团队：气道通气、领导与治疗决定、按压给药记录、药学核查及亲属支持。应迁移团队原则，不假设每支院前队都有全部这些职业。要分工、以闭环确认剂量及动作、保持按压质量并记时间，同时保留患者家属沟通及交接。这是团队演练框架，不是新增药物、起搏或独立医院岗位权限。

00:41:39.336 --> 00:41:52.392
Close the notes and explain the complete route from a forearm vein to tissue delivery and back. Include blood components, valve states and the difference between electrical activation and useful flow.
合上笔记，从前臂静脉讲到组织输送再回来，包含血液成分、瓣膜状态，以及电激动与有用血流的区别。

00:41:52.392 --> 00:42:04.872
Work a fresh cardiac-output example, derive pulse pressure and estimated mean pressure, and explain the ideal half-radius relationship. State the assumptions instead of only giving numbers.
做一个新心排例，算脉压和估平均压，再讲理想半径减半关系。除了结果，还应说明假设。

00:42:04.872 --> 00:42:18.840
Predict cell-water movement across a membrane, compare hydrostatic and oncotic contributions and name the classic model limit. Then explain why an edematous patient can still have poor effective circulation.
预测水跨膜方向，比较静水压及胶体渗透贡献，并说经典模型局限，再解释水肿者为何仍可有效循环差。

00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:37.176
Finally move to the practical station and the ECG lessons. Complete preparation, acquisition and reassessment as one flow. Reading and a successful simulation prepare you; they are not a signed school competency or permission to perform outside actual scope.
最后转到实训站和ECG课，把准备、采集及复评连成一条流程。阅读和模拟能准备你，却不是学校已签能力认证，也不允许超实际范围操作。
